# DEC-730's `delete_with` said a test-only method's spec code tests nothing
# live, but the hunt found it on rows whose own grading says the method may
# be called (a helper Rails mixes into a view, a name config holds, a module
# listed at runtime): deleting those specs loses a test of live code. Only a
# `clear` row plans units.
dead lib Lowered#shine=test-only&~public_send
# What the method reaches was never weighed: `initialize` was exempt
# however much it ran, and the method's own body could call live code or
# read a live constant, so its spec was the only test of that code. Each
# body is weighed now, and one that reaches live code yields no unit.
dead lib Tally#total=test-only& Mention#rewrite=test-only& Mention#slug=test-only&
